{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrT4faWmzVz63VyGncF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, dir='-')` now returns 0, and the right-hand limit still returns `oo`. The `'+-'` direction now raises \"The limit does not exist since left hand limit = 0 and right hand limit = oo\", which is correct. `sympy/series/tests/test_limits.py` passes (175 passed, 3 xfailed). I didn't add a regression test for this case.\n\n`sp.limit(2**x, x, -sp.oo)` already returned 0 in this checkout, so only the `2**(1/x)` case was broken.\n\n**Cause:** for `2**(1/x)` the series expansion fails, so `Limit.doit` falls back to `pow_heuristics`. That helper called `limit(...)` without the `dir` argument, so it always evaluated the right-hand limit.\n\n**Fix:** in `sympy/series/limits.py`, `pow_heuristics` now takes `dir` and passes it to all four inner `limit` calls. The call site in `doit` passes it in."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":25271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"output_tokens":337,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9155adc4-79ba-45e1-a7fc-2355373e1674","uuid":"57a07f8a-fd5b-4c6b-af6e-a92611992a54","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:04:08.699Z","request_id":"req_011ChLrT4XebXFn5irgdryjV"}
